   "The world's first mathematics hackathon!\nThis fall, math enthusiasts from around the world will gather at Caltech and, over 40 hours, with the help of frontier AI models, try to solve open math problems, propose new mathematical theories, and fully explain and re-derive their results to a panel of mathematician judges.\nThey want to explore two questions:\n1️⃣ How much can AI speed up the process of math research, from idea to peer-reviewed publication?\n2️⃣ What will happen to the role of mathematicians as AI gets better and better at finding proofs?\n📌 Event information\n· Dates: October 30 – November 1, 2026\n· Location: California Institute of Technology\n· Format: 40 hours\n· Resources: over US$2 million in AI credits and frontier models\n· Supporters: OpenAI, Anthropic, DARPA expMath, Cognition, Cloudflare, a16z, YC, and others\n👩‍🏫 Invitation for judges and guests\nRound-trip airfare, accommodation during the event, and appearance fees for invited judges are covered by the organizers; an official invitation letter can also be provided if a visa is needed.\n🔗 Participant and judge applications: mathathonchallenge.com/apply…\n🔗 Official website: mathathonchallenge.com"
