 "DcP4Sz4E3rL": {
  "parts": [
   "OpenAI is playing an important card in the enterprise market: even when using the most powerful frontier models, enterprises don't have to give up control over their confidential data\nThe more a model can run long workflows and work autonomously across many interactions, the more security risk is likely to hide in a chain of requests rather than in a single conversation. OpenAI's solution is Private Safety Processing: it lets automated systems recognize patterns of abuse across interactions, without OpenAI staff directly seeing the enterprise's prompts and responses.\nThe enterprise keeps control of its data, and OpenAI receives only limited safety alerts.\nBut don't get the wrong idea: this doesn't mean the conversations of all ChatGPT users instantly become \"zero data retention.\" For now it mainly targets eligible, approved API/enterprise customers.\nThis isn't just a privacy policy — it's a race for trust in enterprise AI: who can make enterprises dare to hand over their most important data while the models get more powerful?"
  ]
 },
